# ouroboros#106 / EigenScript#869: a bare interrogative is refused only when
# its result is DISCARDED (a statement with a POP after it). As the LAST
# statement of a program, a function body or an if-block it is that block's
# value and compiles on both sides. The self-hosted check's first cut flagged
# these too; the gate's must_reject row caught it ("C oracle ACCEPTS").
x is 1
x is 2
define f() as:
    what is x
print of (f of [])
if x > 0:
    who is x
print of 3
